{"review_id":"00001788303359016607-0004098830-000001-cycle-review-1","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:15220b0eb0aba7f106f0c6c53d7f9b11b49d28a841de56c7f39722ff0babc9d6","findings":[{"finding_id":"F1-resolved-model-never-persisted","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Provider-resolved model identity is exposed but never recorded anywhere durable","claim":"The adapter captures the provider-resolved model identity from `message_start.message.model` into `AnthropicAdapter::attempt_metadata`, but nothing in the persistence path ever reads it. `persist_run_outcome` writes `model_identity` from the caller-supplied requested identifier only; the diff threads `provider_request_id` from `AttemptUsage` into `UsageObservation` but adds no equivalent channel for the resolved identity, and `AttemptUsage` has no field for it. The metadata map is adapter-instance-local and is discarded with the adapter, so acceptance criterion 8 ('Model identity records both the requested identifier and the provider-resolved identity when exposed, and a moving alias is never frozen into canonical worker identity') is satisfied only in an in-memory accessor no production caller invokes — the alias is precisely what gets frozen into the persisted worker/usage rows. The integration test `model_alias_resolves_to_a_distinct_dated_identity` asserts on `adapter.attempt_metadata(...)` directly rather than on any persisted row, so the gap is not caught.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -526,7 +527,7 @@ pub fn persist_run_outcome(\n             cli_version: None,\n             model_identity,\n             service_tier: None,\n-            provider_request_id: None,\n+            provider_request_id: provider_request_id.as_deref(),\n             uncached_input_tokens: usage.uncached_input_tokens,\n             cache_read_tokens: usage.cache_read_tokens,\n             cache_write_tokens: usage.cache_write_tokens,"},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":66,"end":75}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:2c0f1fee5e4e7bee6132cf321c0a71a4bfc619c4f31ba1bd58b0c4802e1b7ddd","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":97145,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:225fe60abc5447c1e17a1910bc63bb0eb484063fe054a3af47ad28b3dfa9e6af","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-2c0f1fee5e4e7bee6132cf321c0a71a4bfc619c4f31ba1bd58b0c4802e1b7ddd-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Thread the resolved identity the same way `provider_request_id` was threaded: add a `resolved_model: Option<String>` to `AttemptUsage` (populated in `run_loop` from the adapter outcome or a contract-level field), and record it in `UsageObservation` alongside the requested `model_identity`. Add a daemon-side assertion that a run requesting the alias persists both the alias and the dated snapshot.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F2-refusal-category-not-recorded","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Refusal category is dropped before persistence, and a refusal is indistinguishable from an auth failure in the ledger","claim":"Acceptance criterion 6 requires that a refusal stop record its category as an honest terminal reason. The adapter maps `refusal` to `AdapterStopReason::Refusal { category }`, but `run_loop` collapses it to `StopReason::ProviderFailure { taxonomy: NonRetryable }`, which the daemon persists as the string `provider-failure` — the same value the auth-failure test asserts for a credential failure. The category survives only in `AnthropicAdapter::attempt_metadata`, which no persistence path reads (same channel as F1). Worse, the metadata insert is guarded on `stream_outcome.resolved_model.is_some()`, so a refusal on a stream whose `message_start` carried no model field records no metadata at all and the category is lost even from the in-memory accessor. The net effect is that no durable record distinguishes a safety refusal from any other non-retryable provider failure.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -526,7 +527,7 @@ pub fn persist_run_outcome(\n             cli_version: None,\n             model_identity,\n             service_tier: None,\n-            provider_request_id: None,\n+            provider_request_id: provider_request_id.as_deref(),\n             uncached_input_tokens: usage.uncached_input_tokens,\n             cache_read_tokens: usage.cache_read_tokens,\n             cache_write_tokens: usage.cache_write_tokens,"},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":66,"end":75}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:f9fe0e89ee77d782fa75ed4e111488df3f532116460646b1a1c9386e872b2b0c","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":36795,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:225fe60abc5447c1e17a1910bc63bb0eb484063fe054a3af47ad28b3dfa9e6af","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-f9fe0e89ee77d782fa75ed4e111488df3f532116460646b1a1c9386e872b2b0c-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Record the metadata unconditionally (do not gate the `attempt_metadata` insert on `resolved_model.is_some()`), and give the refusal a distinct persisted terminal reason — either a dedicated loop-level `StopReason` variant or a category column on the evidence/observation row — so a safety refusal is separable from an auth or invalid-request failure in the ledger. Add a daemon test asserting the persisted refusal row carries the provider category.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F3-unbounded-adapter-state","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"`tool_use_registry` and `attempt_metadata` grow without bound for the life of the adapter","claim":"Both maps are inserted into on every streamed tool call and every completed attempt, and neither is ever pruned: `cancel` removes a single `attempt_metadata` entry, and nothing ever removes a `tool_use_registry` entry. Each registry entry retains the tool name, the fully parsed argument JSON, and every preceding thinking block's text plus signature. A daemon that holds one `AnthropicAdapter` across many executions accumulates this for every tool call it has ever seen, with no TTL, capacity bound, or per-execution scope. The module doc frames the registry as adapter-local bookkeeping but does not establish a lifetime for it.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":100,"end":109}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:20dcbf111758d1e54ac4f6e869b35c9081ceede7ed02723cdab8c1640f9eacc3","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:225fe60abc5447c1e17a1910bc63bb0eb484063fe054a3af47ad28b3dfa9e6af","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-20dcbf111758d1e54ac4f6e869b35c9081ceede7ed02723cdab8c1640f9eacc3-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Bound both maps: either scope the adapter (and therefore the registry) to a single loop run, or add explicit eviction — drop a call id once its `tool_result` has been replayed, drop attempt metadata once the host has read it, and cap total entries with LRU eviction. Document the chosen lifetime in the contract's `tool_use` replay section.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F4-contract-contradicts-synthesized-tool-use","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"Normative contract says a malformed call is 'never replayed', but the adapter synthesizes a `tool_use` with empty input","claim":"The contract's 'Malformed or unknown tool calls' section states that the adapter does not populate `tool_use_registry` for an unparseable call and that 'an unrecoverable malformed call is never replayed either.' The implementation's `None` arm in `push_assistant_and_tool_turn` does replay it — it synthesizes a `tool_use` block carrying the call id, the capability name from the tool-result payload, and `input: {}`. The test `refused_malformed_call_never_produces_an_orphan_tool_result_on_the_next_turn` asserts that synthesized block is present, so the code and its own tests agree with each other and disagree with the normative document. The same path also fabricates empty arguments for any call id unknown to a fresh adapter instance replaying persisted history, presenting the model with a record of a call it did not make in that form.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs","range":{"start":308,"end":330}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"docs/contracts/anthropic-adapter.md","range":{"start":105,"end":122}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:f9fe0e89ee77d782fa75ed4e111488df3f532116460646b1a1c9386e872b2b0c","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":36795,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:225fe60abc5447c1e17a1910bc63bb0eb484063fe054a3af47ad28b3dfa9e6af","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-f9fe0e89ee77d782fa75ed4e111488df3f532116460646b1a1c9386e872b2b0c-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Correct the contract to describe what the code actually does — that an unremembered call id is reconstructed as a placeholder `tool_use` with empty input so the `tool_result` is not orphaned — and state plainly that the replayed input is a synthesized placeholder, not the model's original arguments. Alternatively, retain the raw unparsed fragment string for malformed calls so the replayed block reflects what the model emitted.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F5-changes-outside-allowed-paths","category":"scope_violation","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"Five changed files fall outside the task's `allowed_paths` of `crates/`","claim":"The task declares `allowed_paths: [\"crates/\"]` with no prohibited-change carve-outs, but the candidate modifies `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `config/default.toml`, `docs/contracts/providers-index.md`, and adds `docs/contracts/anthropic-adapter.md` — all outside `crates/`. The workspace manifest and lockfile edits are mechanically required by the new `futures-util` dependency and the `reqwest` `stream` feature, but the configuration example block and the two documentation files are substantive additions to paths the task did not open.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"Cargo.toml","hunk":"@@ -54,8 +54,9 @@ async-trait = \"0.1\"\n regex = \"1\"\n once_cell = \"1\"\n ring = \"0.17\"\n-reqwest = { version = \"0.12\", default-features = false, features = [\"rustls-tls\", \"json\", \"blocking\"] }\n+reqwest = { version = \"0.12\", default-features = false, features = [\"rustls-tls\", \"json\", \"blocking\", \"stream\"] }\n wiremock = \"0.6\"\n axum = \"0.8\"\n landlock = \"0.4\"\n wait-timeout = \"0.2\"\n+futures-util = \"0.3\""},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"docs/contracts/providers-index.md","hunk":"@@ -23,3 +23,5 @@ them. Unknown kinds and unknown extension fields fail validation closed.\n   descriptors and the credential non-persistence boundary.\n - [Registry migration](registry-migration.md) — configuration mutation\n   and migration bookkeeping.\n+- [Anthropic adapter](anthropic-adapter.md) — the `anthropic-api` raw\n+  runtime: PRD-058 wire mapping, stop reasons, caching, and billing mode."},{"kind":"file_range","path":"config/default.toml","range":{"start":36,"end":50}}],"remediation":"Either widen the task's `allowed_paths` to cover `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `config/`, and `docs/contracts/` before accepting, or record an explicit exception noting that dependency-manifest, worked-example configuration, and normative-contract files were required by this task and were reviewed as in scope.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F6-adapterstopreason-lost-copy","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"informational","blocking":false,"title":"`AdapterStopReason` silently lost its `Copy` impl while the design note calls the change purely additive","claim":"Adding `Refusal { category: Option<String> }` forced the removal of `Copy` from the public `AdapterStopReason` in the shared contract crate. The contract's Design notes describe the change as '(additive; every existing variant and match arm elsewhere in the workspace was unaffected)', which is accurate about the variant set but not about the type's API surface: dropping `Copy` is a breaking change for any consumer that relied on implicit copies. The workspace happens to compile, so the break is invisible today, but the design note is the artifact a future adapter author will consult and it understates what the extension cost.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/attempt.rs","hunk":"@@ -170,13 +170,24 @@ impl UsageCategories {\n     }\n }\n \n-#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n pub enum AdapterStopReason {\n     EndTurn,\n     ToolUse,\n     MaxTokens,\n     StopSequence,\n     ContentFilter,\n+    /// A provider-side pause requiring the caller to resubmit to continue.\n+    /// Familiar never assumes provider-side resumption of the interrupted\n+    /// request: this is an honest \"continue independently\" signal, distinct\n+    /// from `ToolUse` (which requires a tool round-trip first).\n+    PauseTurn,\n+    /// A safety/content-policy refusal, with the provider's category when\n+    /// exposed. Distinct from `ContentFilter` (a generic content-filter\n+    /// stop with no category) and never conflated with `MaxTokens`.\n+    Refusal {\n+        category: Option<String>,\n+    },\n }\n \n #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"format","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:3d933e1869772210c5da742854ac79bff6948dfed7a3793993b99d6203287dfe","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1343,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-59","revision":"sha256:225fe60abc5447c1e17a1910bc63bb0eb484063fe054a3af47ad28b3dfa9e6af","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-3d933e1869772210c5da742854ac79bff6948dfed7a3793993b99d6203287dfe-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Amend the Design notes to state that `AdapterStopReason` also lost its `Copy` impl, or keep `Copy` by interning the refusal category as a `&'static str` / small enum rather than an owned `String`.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
